-- title:
--   Fibre at p of each Deligne–Rapoport chart: reduced, two components
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime. Inside the field of formal Laurent series $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p` be the subfield generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the $q$-expansions $j(q^{d})$ for the nonzero divisors $d \mid p$, and let $j \in F$ be the element `IgusaScheme.jFull p` given by the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Consider the two $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebras of $F$ attached to this data: $A_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin ℤ F j`, the set of elements of $F$ integral over the subring $\mathbb{Z}[j] =$ `Algebra.adjoin ℤ {j}`, and $A_{\infty} =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgInf ℤ F j`, the set of elements of $F$ integral over $\mathbb{Z}[j^{-1}]$. The theorem asserts four things: the quotient ring $A_{\mathrm{fin}}/pA_{\mathrm{fin}}$ by the ideal generated by the image of $p$ is reduced; the set of minimal primes over the ideal $pA_{\mathrm{fin}}$ has cardinality exactly $2$ (as a `Set.ncard`); and the same two assertions for $A_{\infty}$ and the ideal $pA_{\infty}$.
--
--   The rings $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $A_{\infty}$ are the coordinate rings of the two affine charts whose pushout is the integral model [`ModularCurve.DRModel p`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackage.html#L26) of $X_0(p)$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$, so the statement records, chart by chart, that the fibre at $p$ is reduced with exactly two irreducible components, as in Deligne–Rapoport and Katz–Mazur. It is used in the local analysis of that model at the crossing points of the two components, in particular by the results on stalks and on the images of the two chart embeddings.
